    "title": "Unlocking the Vault - by Carri Twigg and Culture House",
    "text": "Hi friends!!\nI’m limping across the finish line this particular Friday but I made it. and so did you. So congratulations one and all.\nThe biggest developments for us this week was the transition of Nicole Galovski ’s incredible newsletter In The Trenches to a paid newsletter. Now, we’ve been warning ya’ll that this day would come and its finally here. Every other week Nicole is giving out the hard won wisdom as well as practical advice, tips and insights. And now, behind the paywall she’s dropping in the decks, sizzles, budget templates, and materials that we have used to sell, make and distribute our shows and build this business. Its a invaluable offering if you are In The Trenches of entertainment. Upgrade to a paid subscription at the link below:\nHere is a preview of just some of what Nicole had for you all behind the paywall this week:\nFor Paid Subscribers: Comment or DM me and I’ll share the below with you (Reach out and I’m happy to gift a subscription as well!!)\nAttachment Agreement – I can share you on the legal document template we use to attach collaborators during development (essentially when Brie, said “I want to work with Culture House” this is the type of agreement that we all signed together to begin developing a show)\nTHATS RIGHT FRIENDS, Nicole is literally unlocking the vault, showing where we buried our bodies, the blueprint for our triumphs and the route that let us to our failures. Its a gold mine. Share In The Trenches with someone you know who needs the keys!\nWe’re gathering on Monday (1/26) with Moms First for Motherhood Live—a live conversation about culture, power, and the myths used to dismiss mothers. Icons are on the lineup! Including living legend Gloria Steinem.\nRegister HERE and we’ll see you on Monday!\nAccording to recent media narratives, the real danger isn’t broken systems or failed leadership. It’s “organized gangs of wine moms” — women who are standing up, speaking out, and refusing to stay quiet. It’s meant to sound ridiculous. And it is. But it’s also deliberate.\nWhen women show up in public and refuse to be silent, ridicule is always the first line of attack. Labels are used to shrink us. Jokes are used to dismiss us. Panic is manufactured to push us back into our place.\nBut we know better.\nJoin Reshma Saujani, Ilana Glazer, Emily Oster, Anna Malaika Tubbs, Gloria Steinem, Katie Bethell, Shannon Watts and hundreds of other moms for a live conversation decoding the cons meant to shrink moms’ voices.\nThe untold story about how Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. and an all-star team of civil rights activists took to basketball courts to rally young voters while winning hearts of communities, and how their strategy has echoed in contemporary politics. Hoops. Hopes & dreams was the last project of our friend the late Michael Latt, and was brought to life thanks to the tireless determination of Glenn Kaiko (Director, Producer), Michael’s parents and the Michael Latt Legacy Fund, Jesse Williams (Producer), and others.\nIts an inspiring and hopeful reminder in these times of uncertainty and heartache.\nAs always, offering you a way to tap into the mayhem of our political moment with two people who know what they are talking about AND know how to laugh. Watch, like and subscribe 🙂\nThats it for this week!\nHave an amazing weekend\nxo\nCarri, Rae, Nicole and Mikhael\nSource link",
